% publisher. Nothing is guessed. The same list appears in human-readable form at the end of
% paper/draft.md; if you edit one, edit both.
%
% main.tex cites these with \cite{...} and typesets them with \bibliographystyle{unsrt}, so
% entries are numbered by order of first citation. scripts/make_latex.py refuses to build if
% the draft's own numbering disagrees with that order.
%
% Keep `note` fields bibliographic. BibTeX prints them in the reference list, so a reminder
% left in one ("cite the corrected version") appears in the published paper. Reminders about
% an entry belong in a % comment beside it.

